{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"fd7f38b6-4c9a-4197-ae12-4734e91a369e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The root cause has been identified and fixed, with tests added and findings documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-y2cuaq/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n\n* **Cause**: On the first publish, the table is empty, so `similar` is an empty list `[]`. On the second publish, `existing` contains stories, so [`similarity()`](file:///tmp/h-y2cuaq/src/app.py#L25-L31) calculates similarity scores as Python `float` values. DynamoDB (`boto3`) rejects Python `float` values with `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`, causing [`handler()`](file:///tmp/h-y2cuaq/src/app.py#L69-L79) to fail with a 500 error.\n* **Fix**: Converted `similarity()`'s return value to `Decimal(str(round(...)))` in [`src/app.py`](file:///tmp/h-y2cuaq/src/app.py#L31). Added regression tests in [`tests/test_publish.py`](file:///tmp/h-y2cuaq/tests/test_publish.py) to prevent regressions.\n","duration_seconds":50.872747,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":193756,"output_tokens":2484,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":196240}}}
